{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a segment is for."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NetworkSegmentKind","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\""},{"type":"text","text":", never left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to refuse. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/networksegmentkind"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK18NetworkSegmentKindO","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NetworkSegmentKind"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NetworkSegmentKind"}],"title":"NetworkSegmentKind"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/access","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/quarantine","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/unknown"],"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/init(rawValue:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/encode(to:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkSegmentKind\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"relationshipsSe